Priya (Docs): Created a tiny PR to err-ref to add a minimal 'stream-resume' example + header precedence note. PR #8302.
Omar (Eng Docs): Can we keep it super minimal: one sync snippet showing Retry-After vs x-rw-retry parsing, and one stream resume example using resume_token. No imports, include SDK version note.
Jon (SDK): I'll add TS + Python. Note: SDK exposes retryWithBackoff; show it as an option but still include raw header parsing for clarity.
Tess (Runtime): Runtime now attaches resume_token in the stream footer when we cut output due to context overflow. Recommend using that token + kv_cache_hint for best performance.
Priya (Docs): Wording suggestion: "When a stream is truncated, prefer resuming with resume_token to avoid repeating compute; fallback to a fresh request only if resume_token is missing."
Jon (SDK): Draft TS snippet (TS SDK >=3.2):
```ts
// retry helper parses Retry-After then x-rw-retry
async function retrySend(req){
  return await retryWithBackoff(()=>client.generate(req), {tries:3})
}
// streaming resume (pseudo)
async function resumeStream(token){
  return await client.generate({resume_token:token, kv_cache_hint: true})
}
```
Omar (Eng Docs): Add one-line trim guidance: "Trim oldest messages until estimated tokens < model limit; set partial=true while resuming."
Tess (Runtime): Add inline note: pass kv_cache_hint when resuming to improve cache hits; runtime will honor it.
preview-bot: Preview live: https://deploy-preview.redwood/docs/8302 — please review.
Jon (SDK): Pushed Python equivalent and a one-liner about header precedence: 'Retry-After > x-rw-retry'.
Priya (Docs): Thanks — plan to merge tomorrow after quick security link check. Will add a short migration note for Dedicated customers about resume_token semantics.
Omar (Eng Docs): LGTM from docs side; will do a tiny editorial pass post-merge.
Priya (Docs): Merged. Closing thread. :tada:
